.TH "bc_state_set_alias" "3" "2026\-02\-01" "bash\-server 0.1.0" "bash\-server library"
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
#include \f[B]\(dqbashclient.h\(dq\f[R]

int bc_state_set_alias(bc_client_t *c, const char *name,
                       const char *value);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Defines or replaces a shell alias on the bash\-server session associated
with the client connection \f[B]c\f[R].
If an alias with the given name already exists, its expansion value is
replaced.
If it does not exist, a new alias is created.
.PP
The function sends a \f[CR]set\f[R] request on the STATE channel
(\f[CR]CHAN_STATE\f[R], channel 2) with namespace
\f[CR]\(dqalias\(dq\f[R], the alias name, and the expansion value.
The server performs the equivalent of
\f[CR]alias name=\(aqvalue\(aq\f[R] in the shell session.
.PP
The alias takes effect immediately for subsequent command evaluations in
the session, provided that alias expansion is enabled
(\f[CR]shopt \-s expand_aliases\f[R], which is the default for
interactive sessions).
